 "_note": "The SVG PATH-DATA mini-language (`d`) \u2192 the NORMALIZED absolute segment list. THE LAW: every command folds to M / L / C / Q / Z in ABSOLUTE user coordinates \u2014 H and V become L, S and T resolve their reflected control point (the reflection of the previous cubic/quadratic control about the current point; the CURRENT POINT itself when the previous command was not of that family), and an elliptical arc becomes 1..4 cubics through the F.6.5 endpoint\u2192centre conversion, split at ceil(|\u0394\u03b8| / 90\u00b0) with k = 4/3\u00b7tan(\u03b4/4). The F.6.6 corrections are part of the law: rx = |rx|, ry = |ry|; identical endpoints emit NOTHING; a zero radius degenerates to a line; radii too small are scaled by sqrt(\u039b). Numbers follow the SVG number grammar \u2014 exponents, no-space negatives, decimal runs ('.5.5' is two numbers) \u2014 and the two arc FLAGS are single characters, so 'a5 5 0 0110 0' is fa=0 fs=1 x=10 y=0. Implicit repeats: a repeated argument set after M is L (after m, l); every other command repeats itself. ARTICLE 7: a malformed token STOPS the parse, keeps every segment already produced, and emits exactly ONE diagnostic \u2014 never a crash, never a partial number. `bbox` is the TIGHT bounding box (curve extrema solved analytically, never control-point hull) and is EXACT on every renderer \u2014 the geometry half of the determinism split (pixels are toleranced, geometry is not). Expected values come from an independent scratch implementation, never from a kernel under test.",
